---
description: Wire MonoBehaviour refs in the inspector, do not find or add them at runtime
alwaysApply: true
---

# Serialize component references

If a MonoBehaviour needs another component or transform on the same prefab/scene object, declare `[SerializeField]` and assign it in the inspector (or editor setup). Do not `GetComponent`, `AddComponent`, or `Find` in `Awake`/`Start` as a fallback.

```csharp
// BAD
[SerializeField] private Rigidbody _rb;
[SerializeField] private Outline _outline;

private void Awake() {
    if (_rb == null)
        _rb = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
    if (_outline == null)
        _outline = gameObject.AddComponent<Outline>();
}

// GOOD
[SerializeField] private Rigidbody _rb;
[SerializeField] private Outline _outline;
```

Allowed `GetComponent` / `AddComponent`:
- a **one-time** lookup on another object (raycast hit, bind/spawn). Cache the result; never repeat it every frame
- editor setup that **creates** prefabs/scenes
- runtime factories that build a new object and then add its parts

If a per-frame lookup seems unavoidable, ask first. See `no-getcomponent-in-update`.
